UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 460-10-25, a guarantor must recognize a liability at fair value for the stand-ready obligation at inception, regardless of the probability of having to perform. The $30,000 fee received typically approximates the fair value and is recorded as a guarantee obligation, then amortized to revenue over the guarantee period.
Wrong (B): Immediately recognizing the fee as revenue ignores the ongoing stand-ready obligation that ASC 460 requires the guarantor to record as a liability.
Wrong (C): The guarantee obligation is measured at fair value ($30,000), not the full guaranteed loan amount of $2,000,000.
