-- Q11714: Contingencies [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 450-20, the loss contingency accrual represents the estimated settlement or judgment amount, not costs of defending the case. Legal defense costs are expensed as incurred because they relate to services received, not to the contingent loss itself. The predominant practice under GAAP is to expense litigation costs when incurred.
Wrong (A): Adding anticipated defense costs to the accrual conflates defense expenses with the estimated probable loss, overstating the contingent liability.
Wrong (B): Legal fees are not a separate contingent liability; they are period costs expensed as the legal services are rendered.
Wrong (C): Offsetting legal fees against the accrual would understate the probable loss amount, which must reflect the expected settlement or judgment.$EXPL$
