-- Q11715: Contingencies [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 410-20, a legal obligation to retire a tangible long-lived asset (mine restoration) is an asset retirement obligation measured at fair value using present value techniques at initial recognition. The EPA remediation is a loss contingency under ASC 450-20, accrued at the estimated amount because it arises from a contingent environmental event rather than a contractual retirement obligation.
Wrong (A): AROs under ASC 410-20 have distinct recognition rules including mandatory present-value discounting, unlike the undiscounted accrual approach under ASC 450.
Wrong (B): The EPA remediation is not an ARO because it does not arise from a legal obligation to retire a long-lived asset; it stems from environmental contamination.
Wrong (D): The mine restoration is a recognized liability, not merely a disclosed commitment, because a legal obligation to restore the site exists at inception.$EXPL$
