-- Q11717: Contingencies [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 420-10-25, one-time employee termination benefits under an involuntary arrangement are recognized when the plan is communicated to employees and no future service beyond a minimum retention period is required. Since all 80 employees were notified by December 31 with no specified future service period, the full $1,600,000 is accrued.
Wrong (A): Proration applies only when employees must render service beyond a minimum retention period to receive benefits, which is not the case here.
Wrong (C): The 50% allocation has no basis in ASC 420; the full amount is recognized upon communication when no future service requirement exists.
Wrong (D): Waiting until actual termination is incorrect because the liability is recognized when the plan is communicated, not when employees physically depart.$EXPL$
