-- Q11719: Contingencies [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 450-20, contingency accruals must be reassessed each reporting period using the best available information. A settlement offer that management and legal counsel expect to accept represents a better estimate of the probable loss. The accrual is adjusted to $1,350,000 as a change in estimate under ASC 250-10-45.
Wrong (B): Entities must update accruals when new information provides a more reliable estimate; retaining an outdated amount does not comply with ASC 450.
Wrong (C): The settlement offer does not eliminate the probability of loss; it refines the amount, so removing the accrual entirely is unsupported.
Wrong (D): Summing the settlement offer and original estimate double-counts the exposure; only the best current estimate should be accrued.$EXPL$
