Wrong (A): The component approach permits partial accrual rather than requiring all cost elements to be estimable before any recognition occurs.
Wrong (B): Limiting the accrual to investigation costs alone ignores the $280,000 feasibility study costs that are also reasonably estimable.
Wrong (C): Estimating total costs including cleanup is not appropriate here because the actual cleanup costs remain indeterminate and cannot yet be reasonably estimated.$EXPL$
