-- Q11726: Contingencies [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 450-20, contingencies are reassessed each reporting period. When probability changes from remote to probable and the amount becomes reasonably estimable, the full loss is recognized in the current period as a change in estimate under ASC 250-10-45, not as a prior-period adjustment.
Wrong (A): A change in likelihood assessment represents new information constituting a change in estimate, which is accounted for prospectively, not retroactively through restatement.
Wrong (B): When a loss becomes probable and estimable, ASC 450 requires accrual, not mere disclosure; note-only treatment is insufficient.
Wrong (C): Splitting the loss between years has no basis in GAAP; the full amount is recognized when the criteria are first met.$EXPL$
