-- Q11730: Fair Value [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): ASC 820-10-35-54 requires classification based on the lowest level of significant input currently used. When observable inputs become unavailable and management substitutes unobservable assumptions (internal prepayment and default rates), the measurement transfers to Level 3 with required disclosure of amounts, reasons, and gains or losses.
Wrong (B): Classification follows current inputs, not historical ones; retaining Level 2 when observable inputs are no longer significant is incorrect.
Wrong (C): Level 1 requires unadjusted quoted prices in active markets for identical instruments; broker quotes becoming available again would not automatically qualify as Level 1.
Wrong (D): Continuing to measure at Level 2 without adjusting for the actual inputs used misrepresents the measurement''s reliability in the fair value hierarchy.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11730;

-- Q11733: Fair Value [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): ASC 820-10-35-48 defines market-corroborated inputs as those derived principally from or corroborated by observable market data through correlation or other means. These qualify as Level 2 because they are based on observable data even though a model is required.
Wrong (A): Level 1 requires unadjusted quoted prices for identical instruments in active markets; model-derived inputs corroborated by market data do not meet this standard.
Wrong (B): Being model-derived does not automatically make inputs Level 3; inputs corroborated by observable market data are classified as Level 2.
Wrong (C): The use of a correlation model does not make inputs unobservable when the underlying data is derived from observable market sources.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11733;

-- Q11734: Fair Value [hard/L4]
