UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): ASC 825-10-25-3 requires that when the fair value option is elected, upfront costs and fees are recognized in earnings immediately, not deferred or capitalized. The decrease from $10,000,000 to $9,800,000 reduces the liability by $200,000, recognized as a gain in net income.
Wrong (B): Deferring and amortizing issuance costs is incorrect because the fair value option eliminates the ability to capitalize transaction costs; they must be expensed immediately.
Wrong (C): Capitalizing issuance costs as a discount is the treatment for instruments not under the fair value option; netting against the fair value gain is not permitted.
Wrong (D): Fair value changes on liabilities under the fair value option are generally recognized in earnings, not OCI, unless attributable to instrument-specific credit risk under ASC 825-10-45-5.$EXPL$
