  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): ASC 820-10-35-32 classifies the multi-period excess earnings method as an income approach technique because it converts expected future cash flows into a single present value. The MPEEM isolates cash flows attributable to a single intangible by subtracting returns on contributory assets.
Wrong (A): The market approach uses prices from comparable transactions, not projected cash flows; MPEEM relies on entity-specific cash flow projections.
Wrong (C): The cost approach estimates the cost to recreate or replace an asset; MPEEM measures value through expected earnings, not replacement cost.
