Wrong (A): Annual testing is a test for impairment, not a periodic remeasurement to fair value; the recurring classification requires remeasurement each period.
Wrong (B): Describing impairment as a one-time event that never recurs is inaccurate; impairment can occur in multiple periods, but the measurement is still nonrecurring.
