  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): ASC 820-10-05-1B specifies that fair value is measured at a specific point in time -- the measurement date, typically the balance sheet date. Fair value reflects current market conditions as of that date, not averaged or historical values.
Wrong (A): Fair value is a point-in-time measurement, not an average over multiple quarter-end dates during the fiscal year.
