-- Q11743: Fair Value [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): ASC 820-10-35-10B requires that nonfinancial asset fair value assume the highest and best use by market participants, even if the entity uses the asset differently. The $8.5 million reflects how market participants would deploy the patent through licensing. Defensive use is entity-specific intent, not a market participant assumption.
Wrong (A): ASC 820 prohibits basing nonfinancial asset fair value solely on entity-specific intent; the highest-and-best-use premise governs measurement.
Wrong (C): Averaging entity-specific value and market participant value has no basis in ASC 820; fair value is determined solely from the market participant perspective.
Wrong (D): A marketability discount is not appropriate here because the premise of valuation already assumes the highest and best use by market participants who would license the patent.$EXPL$
